    "slug": "4g-lte-vs-5g-which-is-the-best-router-investment-for-mexico",
    "title": "4G/LTE vs. 5G: What is the best investment in routers for Mexico?",
    "date": "2024-08-22T17:57:22",
    "author": "Daniel Ayala",
    "categories": [
      "Cellular Internet"
    ],
    "excerpt": "Although 5G promises revolutionary speeds, the infrastructure in the country is still developing, so many companies prefer to stick with 4G/LTE technology to ensure their connectivity. Is it time to take the leap?",
    "content": "<p>With the growing attention towards 5G technology and its promises of incredible speeds and ultra-low latencies, it's easy to get carried away with the enthusiasm. However, in Mexico, 5G infrastructure is still under development. Below, we explore whether it is worth taking the leap towards this technology, or if 4G/LTE is still the best choice for your company.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4><strong>Broad and Reliable Coverage</strong></h4>\n\n\n\n<p>In Mexico, 4G/LTE coverage is significantly more extensive and reliable than 5G. While 5G networks are expanding, they are still concentrated in urban and specific areas. In contrast, 4G/LTE covers virtually the entire country, including rural and remote areas, making it the most suitable option for companies that operate outside of large cities or in multiple locations.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4><strong>Solid Performance in a Real Environment</strong></h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Although 5G promises higher speeds and lower latency, in practice the difference is not always so noticeable for many business applications. 4G/LTE still offers more than enough speeds for most business uses, such as video conferencing, cloud access, and point-of-sale systems. Plus, its proven reliability ensures consistent, uninterrupted performance – crucial for keeping operations online.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4><strong>Affordable Costs and Efficiency</strong></h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Deploying 5G is expensive, and these costs are reflected in service prices. By comparison, 4G/LTE technology is much more established, meaning its service costs are lower and more predictable. This is especially important for small and medium-sized businesses (SMEs) in Mexico, which seek to maximize return on investment without sacrificing service quality.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4><strong>Compatibility and Ease of Implementation</strong></h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Most current devices on the market are fully 4G/LTE compatible, reducing the need for costly upgrades or infrastructure changes, while 5G devices exceed the price significantly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4><strong>A Proven and Scalable Solution</strong></h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Mexican companies that need connectivity in areas where infrastructure is limited or where reliability is crucial, find 4G/LTE a robust solution. It is a scalable technology that can grow with business needs, allowing for seamless expansion to new locations without compromising network performance.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4><strong>An Encouraging Future</strong></h4>\n\n\n\n<p>While 5G represents the future of connectivity, 4G/LTE remains the reliable and efficient present in Mexico. For most businesses, especially those outside of large urban centers or looking for a cost-effective and robust solution, 4G/LTE is undoubtedly the best option. With extensive coverage, affordable costs, and proven performance, this technology continues to lead as the preferred choice for keeping businesses connected and operational.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>In <strong>Vialterna</strong> We have personalized plans for each business sector, if you are interested in learning more about <a href=\"/en/insights/4g-lte-vs-5g-which-is-the-best-router-investment-for-mexico/\">click here.</a> </p>",
